          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider a figure with radial arms having exactly 7 angles of symmetry. What will be its smallest angle of symmetry? Is the number of degrees a whole number in this case? If not, express it as a mixed faction.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.15,
            0.646,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us find the angles of symmetry for other kinds of figures.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.168,
            0.306,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "360^{\\circ} \\div 7 = 51\\frac{3}{7}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.203,
            0.593,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "No, its smallest angle of symmetry is not a whole number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.257,
            0.233,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": [
